(926725, 106199, 16488, '<td valign="top">There are many things that could be done to improve this.  This image is over-exposed losing all important detail--it seems that post-processing could have altered that.  It''s also grainy, since it was shot in the shade I suspect the ISO was a bit too high.  Compositionally, the background is distracting, the parked cars demand too much attention.  The object that is truly "stopped" is the basketball, and though the boy''s attention is on it (and therefore the viewer''s attention) we can''t see all of it.  Finally, the context feels a bit off too,  why is he dribbling on the grass lawn?  A worthy subject, hope you take critique well and try again.</td>', 'There are many things that could be done to improve this.  This image is over-exposed losing all important detail--it seems that post-processing could have altered that.  It''s also grainy, since it was shot in the shade I suspect the ISO was a bit too high.  Compositionally, the background is distracting, the parked cars demand too much attention.  The object that is truly "stopped" is the basketball, and though the boy''s attention is on it (and therefore the viewer''s attention) we can''t see all of it.  Finally, the context feels a bit off too,  why is he dribbling on the grass lawn?  A worthy subject, hope you take critique well and try again.', '2004-09-26 14:50:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(926727, 106353, 25143, '<td valign="top">the lighting is not very interesting - there is a lack of visual depth</td>', 'the lighting is not very interesting - there is a lack of visual depth', '2004-09-26 14:51:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(926729, 106287, 4517, '<td valign="top">I like this one, looks dark and scary. 9</td>', 'I like this one, looks dark and scary. 9', '2004-09-26 14:52:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(926730, 106353, 16488, '<td valign="top">The choice of point-of-view is commendable.  However because the focus is so off it doesn''t work well.  As you know there are many similar subjects in this challenge, I''m sure there will be plenty of "how they did its" after the challenge to learn from.</td>', 'The choice of point-of-view is commendable.  However because the focus is so off it doesn''t work well.  As you know there are many similar subjects in this challenge, I''m sure there will be plenty of "how they did its" after the challenge to learn from.', '2004-09-26 14:53:23.000000', NULL, 1),
