(927249, 106208, 16493, '<td valign="top">This was on first try, there was a second try but then the clothes where all wet and it did not look as good then. She was all red on her back after the socond fall.</td>', 'This was on first try, there was a second try but then the clothes where all wet and it did not look as good then. She was all red on her back after the socond fall.', '2004-09-27 01:14:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(927250, 106111, 22734, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your 8th placing with this unique coloration.</td>', 'Congratulations on your 8th placing with this unique coloration.', '2004-09-27 01:14:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(927251, 105171, 93, '<td valign="top">Ok.. for everyone that was wondering.. I DIDN''T CHEAT.. exactly.<br/> <br/>I wasn''t throwing the dart at the dartboard, but instead, was dropping it ON to the dart-board.  However, it wasn''t an easy shot to do still, and I have a couple of outtakes to show you.  <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=108112" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/93/thumb/108112.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/93/thumb/108112.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/93/thumb/108112.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>This is an outtake of the shot I submitted... showing a slightly weaker compositional shot.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=108113" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/93/thumb/108113.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/93/thumb/108113.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/93/thumb/108113.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>This is an outtake from when I *DID* capture the dart after it was thrown (by my roomate). However, because of the background on this one, (plus the other dart), I chose to re-do the shots the way I did them instead.<br/> <br/>Anyway, so I did capture the dart *in* mid-flight.. there were no strings.. I didn''t balance it on anything, no tricks.  It was moving toward the dart board, and I took over 200 shots to freeze it where I did, and finally get what I wanted.<br/> <br/>Thank you to everyone that made this my highest placing entry, that gave me the highest rated shot for my camera, and generally made me feel really good :)</td>', 'Ok.. for everyone that was wondering.. I DIDN''T CHEAT.. exactly. I wasn''t throwing the dart at the dartboard, but instead, was dropping it ON to the dart-board.  However, it wasn''t an easy shot to do still, and I have a couple of outtakes to show you.     This is an outtake of the shot I submitted... showing a slightly weaker compositional shot.   This is an outtake from when I *DID* capture the dart after it was thrown (by my roomate). However, because of the background on this one, (plus the other dart), I chose to re-do the shots the way I did them instead. Anyway, so I did capture the dart *in* mid-flight.. there were no strings.. I didn''t balance it on anything, no tricks.  It was moving toward the dart board, and I took over 200 shots to freeze it where I did, and finally get what I wanted. Thank you to everyone that made this my highest placing entry, that gave me the highest rated shot for my camera, and generally made me feel really good :)', '2004-09-27 01:15:02.000000', NULL, 0),
