(935824, 105855, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi from the Critique Club</b> <br/>...............................................<br/> <br/>This is clearly a superb photo. The key to its success in my view is that you got close to the action so that the viewer feels involved. You have captured brilliantly lots of detail and were round far enough to get the face in view.<br/> <br/>The composition is strong too. If there is any fault then it may be that the background does not hold much interest. Perhaps if the bird had a target in view or if the scenery was particularly beautiful it would have helped.<br/> <br/>The bird''s stance is particularly interesting though, showing a nice fan of feathers and nice feet!<br/> <br/>All the best<br/>Jon</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club ............................................... This is clearly a superb photo. The key to its success in my view is that you got close to the action so that the viewer feels involved. You have captured brilliantly lots of detail and were round far enough to get the face in view. The composition is strong too. If there is any fault then it may be that the background does not hold much interest. Perhaps if the bird had a target in view or if the scenery was particularly beautiful it would have helped. The bird''s stance is particularly interesting though, showing a nice fan of feathers and nice feet! All the bestJon', '2004-10-01 21:40:00.000000', NULL, 0),
