(939385, 106110, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique club:<br/> <br/>It is amazing the shapes that one can find in these type of images.<br/>This is a genre which has been quite overworked, yet you managed to add that new twist. It requires the viewer to really look because many will dismiss it as another droplet study.<br/> <br/>You did very good because you did create a psychedelic effect with the colors. Also the composition is pleasing. I mean the eyes keep coming back to the droplet where it finds safety. The image has an effervercent feel and one can almost feel the gyrations of the movement.<br/> <br/>There is nothing I can say to improve on it, except to congratulate you and to try other variations on different concepts. You work here is admirable. Such applications hone your senses and often give birth to new creations.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-03 22:24:09.</i></td>', 'from the critique club: It is amazing the shapes that one can find in these type of images.This is a genre which has been quite overworked, yet you managed to add that new twist. It requires the viewer to really look because many will dismiss it as another droplet study. You did very good because you did create a psychedelic effect with the colors. Also the composition is pleasing. I mean the eyes keep coming back to the droplet where it finds safety. The image has an effervercent feel and one can almost feel the gyrations of the movement. There is nothing I can say to improve on it, except to congratulate you and to try other variations on different concepts. You work here is admirable. Such applications hone your senses and often give birth to new creations.', '2004-10-03 23:22:24.000000', '2004-10-03 23:24:09.000000', 0),
(939393, 106355, 24896, '<td valign="top"><br/> <br/>I had a good long look at this pic and the others from your port. I wont waste my time here as it seems you don''t need the comments. Great pic. Just a side note even though I''m new here. If the comments made from this site are generally unhelpful to you...PLEASE dont click the Critique box so others that need the critique might have a chance for one.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by HBunch - This comment was NOT from the Crit Club.</i></td>', ' I had a good long look at this pic and the others from your port. I wont waste my time here as it seems you don''t need the comments. Great pic. Just a side note even though I''m new here. If the comments made from this site are generally unhelpful to you...PLEASE dont click the Critique box so others that need the critique might have a chance for one.Message edited by HBunch - This comment was NOT from the Crit Club.', '2004-10-03 23:30:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(939438, 105975, 24896, '<td valign="top">Hi Bill,<br/>Scott here from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>First congratulations on your 19th place finish and your third highest scoring pic. A great capture, perfect focus and DOF.  I do see a couple of things that I would have voted this pic higher for. As is I voted a 5. For me a 5 is - meets the challenge and is technically sound. <br/> <br/>Because this was a Members challenge with Advanced editing rules. I think the board could have been a lot cleaner. Clearing up all of the black and white flecks would have helped a lot for me.<br/> <br/>The red shaft and red and blue flight kinda blend into the colours of the board.  Something more contrasting and flashy would have added some "POP" for me.<br/> <br/>So a good all-around pic, just needed a little more wow for me.<br/>I had a good look through your port and really like the creativity in your work. Keep up the good work and more ribbons will defiantly come.<br/> <br/>I hope my critique helps; I know it helped me to reinforce the details in my own work.  If there are any questions/comments you would like on a particular aspect of you pic please feel free to PM me.<br/>Scott <br/> <br/>edit spelling<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-03 23:52:56.</i></td>', 'Hi Bill,Scott here from the Critique Club... First congratulations on your 19th place finish and your third highest scoring pic. A great capture, perfect focus and DOF.  I do see a couple of things that I would have voted this pic higher for. As is I voted a 5. For me a 5 is - meets the challenge and is technically sound.  Because this was a Members challenge with Advanced editing rules. I think the board could have been a lot cleaner. Clearing up all of the black and white flecks would have helped a lot for me. The red shaft and red and blue flight kinda blend into the colours of the board.  Something more contrasting and flashy would have added some "POP" for me. So a good all-around pic, just needed a little more wow for me.I had a good look through your port and really like the creativity in your work. Keep up the good work and more ribbons will defiantly come. I hope my critique helps; I know it helped me to reinforce the details in my own work.  If there are any questions/comments you would like on a particular aspect of you pic please feel free to PM me.Scott  edit spelling', '2004-10-04 00:09:31.000000', '2004-10-04 00:52:56.000000', 0),
(939458, 106110, 26475, '<td valign="top">graphicfunk;<br/> <br/>thank you so much for your comments. It amazes me that I get nothing but good reactions to my images from you, and I am humbled evertime I look at your work in relation to my own.<br/> <br/>Thank you again. I can not thank you enough.<br/> <br/>Stephanie</td>', 'graphicfunk; thank you so much for your comments. It amazes me that I get nothing but good reactions to my images from you, and I am humbled evertime I look at your work in relation to my own. Thank you again. I can not thank you enough. Stephanie', '2004-10-04 00:21:26.000000', NULL, 0),
